## What's in App.tsx right now

Key components in order:
- **Types:** `Tier`, `Screen`, `TaskList`, `Task`, `ArchivedTask`, `Reminder`, `ThemeTokens`
- **`useSwipeToDismiss(onDismiss)`** — reusable hook. Returns `{ dragY, panHandlers }`. Attach `panHandlers` to the sheet handle bar, combine `dragY` with `slideAnim` via `Animated.add()`. 80px threshold to dismiss, springs back on short drags.
- **`useIsPaid()`** — ⚠️ stubbed `return true`. Replace with react-native-iap before Play Store upload.
- **`ReminderPicker`** — shared by EditSheet and PriorityPicker. Day spinner + time picker on one row (side by side, centered). Fixed widths on dynamic elements so layout never shifts. No quick-pick pills (removed — redundant).
- **`EditSheet`** — swipe-to-dismiss on handle. Keyboard tracked via `useState` + Keyboard listeners; ScrollView shrinks to 320 when keyboard up. Text input focused via ref + 320ms setTimeout.
- **`ListActionSheet`** — swipe-to-dismiss. Rename input focused via ref + 220ms setTimeout. Opens via pencil button OR long-press on list pill (400ms hold without movement). No longer has star/pin row.
- **`PriorityPicker`** — swipe-to-dismiss.
- **`ConfirmDialog`** — swipe-to-dismiss.
- **`ProUpsellSheet`** — swipe-to-dismiss.
- **`CalendarSheet`** — swipe-to-dismiss.
- **`DraggablePill`** — individual pill component. Owns its own `PanResponder`. Long-press 400ms + move > 6px = drag; long-press 400ms + release in place = open sheet; tap = select.
- **`ListPillRow`** — renders `DraggablePill` list in a `ScrollView`. Owns shared drag state (`dragX`, `dragIndexRef`, `hoverIndexRef`). Scroll disabled during drag. `onReorder` saves new order to `tri_list_order`.
- **`InputBar`** — `blurOnSubmit={true}` + `Keyboard.dismiss()` on submit.
- **`scheduleReminder()`** — checks `AndroidNotificationSetting.ENABLED`; redirects to system alarm settings if missing. `SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM` in manifest is intentional and fine for Play Store.
- **`Settings`** — Default Tier row removed from UI (state kept for AI fallback). Appearance section: Dark Mode toggle, Theme picker (7 presets + Custom…), Accent picker (Default + 7 presets + Custom…). Both rows are horizontal scrollable card grids with mini-mockup previews.
- **`ScrollableCardBox`** — horizontal scroll container with persistent custom accent-colored scrollbar at the bottom and idle-based "Swipe for more" pulse hint (appears after 3s of no scroll activity, hides on touch/scroll).
- **`MiniMockupPreview`** — faithful tiny render of the task screen (header, edit btn, count, date, list pills, tier divider, task row with priority bar + circle + edit btn) used inside theme/accent cards. Drawn with theme tokens + given accent color.
- **Theme system** — 7 themes × light/dark variants, 11 accents. AsyncStorage: `tri_theme`, `tri_accent_light`, `tri_accent_dark`. Legacy `tri_accent` auto-migrates to `tri_accent_dark` on first load. Old theme IDs remap via `LEGACY_THEME_IDS` (navy→glacier, forest→evergreen, maroon→rosewood, burnt→obsidian, plum→royalplum). Picking a theme auto-resets accent to that theme's curated default. Tapping the active accent again reverts to default. Themes carry `secondary` token used for active list pill bg tint so themes feel like 3-color palettes.
- **`Onboarding`** — ⚠️ OUTDATED. Needs rewrite before Play Store push. Step 1 claims "no projects, no labels" which is wrong now that lists exist.
- **`TriorityApp`** — root state, holds `lists[]` and `activeListId`.

