## Reanimated / draggable-flatlist dead end (do not retry)

Attempted `react-native-draggable-flatlist` → requires `react-native-reanimated` → reanimated 4 requires `react-native-worklets` separately → worklets runtime fails to initialize on RN 0.85 + New Arch. Reanimated 3.x has Java compile errors against RN 0.85's removed Old Arch APIs. Both paths are dead ends. Custom PanResponder solution is the right approach for this project.

---

## ⚠️ Known Issues — Custom Color Pickers (next session must fix before shipping)

The custom accent and theme pickers are wired up and partially working but NOT shippable. Do not mark done until all three are resolved.

### 1. Gesture conflict — wheel unusable
The `HSBColorWheel` outer View uses a single unified `PanResponder` that zones into ring vs. square on first touch. The zone logic is correct but the gesture still fights the parent modal's `useSwipeToDismiss` panHandlers on the drag handle. Result: dragging on the wheel sometimes triggers sheet dismiss, and the ring/square zone detection misfires near the seam between ring and square.

**Recommended fix:** Add `onStartShouldSetPanResponderCapture: () => true` on the wheel's outer View so it claims the gesture before the parent handle bar can. Also wrap the wheel in a `View` with `onStartShouldSetResponder={() => true}` to stop bubbling.

**Alternate fix (simpler, Ross approved):** Replace the wheel entirely with 3 labeled sliders — Hue (0–360), Saturation (0–100), Brightness (0–100). Each is a horizontal track + draggable thumb, single PanResponder per slider, no geometry math. No gesture conflict possible. Ross said: "im ok with sliders for both."

### 2. Layout overflow — content taller than sheet
`CustomThemeSheet` stacks: handle + header row (title + tiny unusable mini-preview) + element pills + wheel + buttons. This overflows on most phones. The mini-preview in the header is meaninglessly small at that size.

**Fix:** Remove header mini-preview entirely. Show title only. Use the color swatch on each pill as feedback. Height budget with wheel at 220px: handle(24) + title(40) + pills(60) + wheel(220) + buttons(60) + padding ≈ 420px — fits without overflow.

### 3. Wheel color prop sync lag on element switch
When user taps a different element pill, `color` prop changes. The wheel updates `hsbRef` during render via `prevColorRef` but doesn't call `setHsb`, so the thumb renders at wrong position for one frame.

**Fix:** Add `useEffect` watching `color` that calls `setHsb(hexToHsb(color))` to force thumb re-render when element switches.

